{
  "schema_version": "argument_graph/0.1",
  "example_id": "persuade:656C7C849144",
  "root": "c5",
  "units": [
    {
      "id": "c1",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 99,
      "text": "When electing the president of the United States, you must vote in favor of the president you want.",
      "role": "lead",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c2",
      "start": 100,
      "end": 198,
      "text": "However, instead of coming down to popular vote, the system uses the Electrolar College to decide.",
      "role": "lead",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c3",
      "start": 199,
      "end": 388,
      "text": "The Electroral Vote works in that the people of a certain states votes for their candidate and the majority of people who vote for a certain president give their votes to a slate of voters.",
      "role": "lead",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c4",
      "start": 389,
      "end": 518,
      "text": "What this means is that the popular vote within a state wins the electoral votes of the electors who then vote for the president.",
      "role": "lead",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c5",
      "start": 519,
      "end": 568,
      "text": "Many people dislike this system including myself.",
      "role": "position",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c6",
      "start": 569,
      "end": 595,
      "text": "I disaprove of this system",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c7",
      "start": 596,
      "end": 629,
      "text": "because it limits representation,",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c8",
      "start": 630,
      "end": 663,
      "text": "permits the disintrest of voters,",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c9",
      "start": 664,
      "end": 708,
      "text": "and reduces a candidates intrest in a state.",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c10",
      "start": 710,
      "end": 816,
      "text": "One major problem with the Electoral College voting system is that it limits representation of the people.",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c11",
      "start": 817,
      "end": 942,
      "text": "The Electoral COllege votes work so that the population of a state directly effects the amount of votes that states recieves.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c12",
      "start": 943,
      "end": 993,
      "text": "For example, Wyoming only has about 500,000 voters",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c13",
      "start": 994,
      "end": 1041,
      "text": "so it only recieves one electoral college vote.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c14",
      "start": 1042,
      "end": 1085,
      "text": "Because there is only one vote for wyoming,",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c15",
      "start": 1086,
      "end": 1190,
      "text": "the 500,000 voters do not have acurate representation in a vote that has a total of 270 electoral votes.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c16",
      "start": 1191,
      "end": 1264,
      "text": "There have also been times in which a president has won the piopular vote",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c16b",
      "start": 1265,
      "end": 1301,
      "text": "but lost the Electoral College vote.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c17",
      "start": 1302,
      "end": 1352,
      "text": "This was seen in the 2000 vote of Bush versus Gore",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c17b",
      "start": 1353,
      "end": 1383,
      "text": "when Gore won the popular vote",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c17c",
      "start": 1384,
      "end": 1416,
      "text": "and Bush won the electoral vote.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c18",
      "start": 1418,
      "end": 1433,
      "text": "One might claim",
      "role": "counterclaim",
      "stance": "reported",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c19",
      "start": 1434,
      "end": 1516,
      "text": "that because the amount of electoral votes for a state is based of the population,",
      "role": "counterclaim",
      "stance": "reported",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c20",
      "start": 1517,
      "end": 1528,
      "text": "it is fair.",
      "role": "counterclaim",
      "stance": "conceded",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c21",
      "start": 1529,
      "end": 1582,
      "text": "However, I believe that the popular vote is more fair",
      "role": "rebuttal",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c22",
      "start": 1583,
      "end": 1632,
      "text": "because it expresses the opinion of the majority.",
      "role": "rebuttal",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c23",
      "start": 1633,
      "end": 1712,
      "text": "In some states, there is a large majority of people running for a single party.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c24",
      "start": 1713,
      "end": 1809,
      "text": "This can be observed primarily in Texas where an overwhelming majority of voters are Republican.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c25",
      "start": 1810,
      "end": 1886,
      "text": "Therefore, the Republican president wins Texas almost every election period.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c26",
      "start": 1887,
      "end": 1942,
      "text": "This can be frustrating for Democrats who live in Texas",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c27",
      "start": 1943,
      "end": 1992,
      "text": "because they know that their vote does not matter",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c28",
      "start": 1993,
      "end": 2052,
      "text": "causing them to lose interest in voting in the first place.",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c29",
      "start": 2053,
      "end": 2086,
      "text": "This is not fair for those people",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c30",
      "start": 2087,
      "end": 2147,
      "text": "nor is it particularly good to express as an American trait.",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c31",
      "start": 2149,
      "end": 2255,
      "text": "As stated before, the larger the population of a states, the more Electoral College votes that state gets.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c32",
      "start": 2256,
      "end": 2339,
      "text": "This leads to a small group of \"big states\" that have such a large amount of votes,",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c33",
      "start": 2340,
      "end": 2411,
      "text": "they are the target for candidates to try to persuade to vote for them.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c35",
      "start": 2412,
      "end": 2508,
      "text": "On the opposite side of the spectrum, most of the other 50 states have a smaller amount of votes",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c36",
      "start": 2509,
      "end": 2564,
      "text": "and are less of an objective for candidates to acquire.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c34",
      "start": 2565,
      "end": 2745,
      "text": "In many states throughout an election preiod (the period in which candidates move to diferent states giving speeches) the candidates never make an appearance in their state at all.",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c37",
      "start": 2746,
      "end": 2863,
      "text": "This is observed in the 2000 election in which seventeen states did not have the candidate make an appearance at all.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c38",
      "start": 2864,
      "end": 2921,
      "text": "This also can lower interest in voting for the president.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c39",
      "start": 2923,
      "end": 3007,
      "text": "The Electoral college voting system is not fair in the way the present system works.",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c40",
      "start": 3008,
      "end": 3069,
      "text": "The system does not show proper representation of the people,",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c41",
      "start": 3070,
      "end": 3106,
      "text": "does not promote interest in voting,",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c42",
      "start": 3107,
      "end": 3206,
      "text": "and causes a candidate to ignore the states in which do not have a large amount of electoral votes.",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c43",
      "start": 3207,
      "end": 3260,
      "text": "Moving to popular vote will fix all of these problems",
      "role": "unannotated",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "c44",
      "start": 3261,
      "end": 3312,
      "text": "and will improve the way we vote for our president.",
      "role": "unannotated",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    }
  ],
